{
  "_id": "c6cf160808f912de",
  "name": "Forgemaster's Armor",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/equipment/chest/breastplate-banded-steel-grey.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Starting when you choose this path at 3rd level, you gain the ability to transform a set of light or medium armor into your Forgemaster's Armor over the course of a long rest. The chosen armor remains as your Forgemaster's Armor until you die, or until you use this ability to make another suit of armor.</p>\n<p>When you create this armor, choose a damage type from the following list: bludgeoning, piercing, slashing, fire, lightning, thunder, acid, or cold.</p>\n<p>While you are wearing your Forgemaster's Armor, you gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You gain a +1 bonus to your AC.</li>\n<li>You can use a bonus action to make one melee weapon attack with your armor against a target within 5 feet of you. If the attack hits, the armor deals 1d6 damage of the type you chose. You use your Strength modifier for the attack and damage rolls.</li>\n<li>When you grapple a creature, the target takes 1d6 damage of the chosen type if your grapple check succeeds.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The damage die of both the bonus action attack and grapple abilities increases to 1d8 at 6th level, 1d10 at 10th level, and 1d12 at 14th level.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
